🤖 ADK — Agent Development Kit

ADK stands for Agent Development Kit.

In simple words:

ADK is Google's framework for building AI Agents using code.

Instead of creating a normal chatbot that only answers questions, ADK helps you build an AI agent that can think about a task, use tools, call other agents, remember information, and complete the task.

🧒 Simple example

Imagine you ask:

"Find me a good hotel in Chennai for tomorrow and tell me the price."

A normal chatbot may simply give you information it already knows.

An ADK Agent can be designed to:

User
  ↓
ADK AI Agent
  ↓
Understand request
  ↓
Use hotel-search tool
  ↓
Get hotel information
  ↓
Compare prices
  ↓
Give recommendation

So the important idea is:

LLM + Instructions + Tools + Agent logic = AI Agent

