🐍 Very Simple ADK Code

A basic ADK agent can look conceptually like this:

from google.adk.agents import Agent

root_agent = Agent(
    name="business_consultant",
    model="gemini-2.5-flash",
    instruction="""
    You are a business consultant.
    Analyze business problems and provide
    practical recommendations.
    """
)

Here:

| Code          | Meaning                              |
| ------------- | ------------------------------------ |
| `Agent()`     | Creates an AI Agent                  |
| `name`        | Name of your agent                   |
| `model`       | LLM used by the agent                |
| `instruction` | Tells the agent what role to perform |
| `root_agent`  | Main/starting agent                  |


=========

🛠️ ADK becomes powerful when you add Tools

For example:

from google.adk.agents import Agent

def calculate_profit(revenue, cost):
    return revenue - cost

root_agent = Agent(
    name="business_consultant",
    model="gemini-2.5-flash",
    instruction="""
    You are a business consultant.
    Analyze sales and profit problems.
    Use the profit calculator when necessary.
    """,
    tools=[calculate_profit]
)

Now the agent can decide:

"I need to calculate profit."

and call:

calculate_profit()

rather than simply guessing the answer.

