🤖 ADK and Multi-Agent

This is where ADK becomes especially interesting for Agentic AI.

You can create multiple specialized agents:

                 Main Agent
                     │
        ┌────────────┼────────────┐
        ↓            ↓            ↓
   Sales Agent   Marketing Agent  Finance Agent
        │            │            │
        ↓            ↓            ↓
   Sales Data    Market Data    Profit Data
        └────────────┼────────────┘
                     ↓
               Final Report

For example:

User:

"Should I expand my textile business?"

The main agent could delegate:

Sales Agent
→ analyzes sales

Finance Agent
→ analyzes profit/cash flow

Marketing Agent
→ analyzes market opportunities

Then the main agent combines everything:

"Based on sales, financial health and market demand, expansion is recommended."

=========

ADK is Google's developer framework for building, orchestrating, testing, and deploying AI agents that can use models, tools, and other agents to accomplish tasks.

For your current Vertex AI / Google Cloud learning, think of the relationship as:

Google Cloud
     ↓
Agent Platform
     ↓
ADK
     ↓
Build AI Agents
     ↓
Tools + RAG + Multi-Agent
     ↓
Evaluation
     ↓
Deployment
     ↓
Monitoring

So ADK is the "development kit" you use to actually build the AI Agent, while Agent Platform is the broader Google Cloud environment 
where you can develop, evaluate, deploy, and operate those agents.


